Package: rbr.simulation.study
Title: A Simulation Study on the Stability and Recovery Behaviour of a
    Relative Belief Ratio Filter for Binary Feature Selection
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Maher", "Emarly", email = "maheremarly1@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Ayman", "Alzaatreh", role = "aut"),
    person("Luai", "Al-Labadi", role = "aut"),
    person("Firuz", "Kamalov", role = "aut"))
Description: Code for the paper of the same name (preprint,
    doi:10.21203/rs.3.rs-10883318/v1). A controlled Monte Carlo study of the
    relative belief ratio filter against Information Gain, Symmetrical
    Uncertainty, mRMR, ReliefF and Boruta, on synthetic data where the
    informative, redundant and noise features are fixed by construction. Seven
    data-generating scenarios, four design cells varying sample size and
    dimensionality one factor at a time, and 300 independent datasets per cell
    and scenario. Reports informative-feature recovery, noise FDR, and selection
    stability by the Jaccard and Kuncheva indices. This is a research project,
    not an installable package: the modules in R/ are sourced by the entry
    points in scripts/.
